## 7. PIPELINE ARCHITECTURE — 13 STEPS

The daily pipeline runs in this exact order. Never reorder steps.

Step 1:  Fetch candles        — NIFTY50 + ^NSEI + ^INDIAVIX
Step 2:  Validate data        — gap detection using NSE holiday calendar
Step 3:  Compute indicators   — NIFTY50 + ^NSEI only (not ^INDIAVIX)
Step 4:  Extract features     — NIFTY50 only (is_liquid, is_ranging, z_score_20d, adaptive RSI/volume)
Step 5:  Compute adaptive thresholds — if ADAPTIVE_THRESHOLDS_ENABLED
Step 6:  Market regime check  — returns BULLISH / SIDEWAYS / BEARISH / HIGH_VOLATILITY
         IF HIGH_VOLATILITY: GOTO Step 12 (skip all signal generation)
Step 7:  Run strategies       — BULLISH/SIDEWAYS: 4 long strategies; BEARISH: 2 short strategies
Step 8:  Fundamental filter   — pass/fail gate, fail-open if no data
Step 9:  Sentiment filter     — RSS fetch only for symbols still in raw_signals
Step 10: Score + deduplicate + position sizing
Step 11: Store signals + create paper trades
Step 12: Update signal statuses (LONG and SHORT lifecycle differ)
Step 13: Update paper trade statuses

Market regime routing:
- BULLISH       => Trend Pullback, Breakout, Range, Mean Reversion (BUY/LONG)
- SIDEWAYS      => Range, Mean Reversion only (BUY/LONG)
- BEARISH       => Trend Pullback SHORT, Breakdown SHORT (SELL/SHORT)
- HIGH_VOLATILITY => No signals at all

SLA: full pipeline must complete within 7 minutes.
Per-symbol timeout: 10 seconds — log warning and skip, do not abort pipeline.

