## 21. FRONTEND ABSOLUTE RULES — NEVER VIOLATE

1. No any. Use unknown and narrow explicitly. noImplicitAny: true in tsconfig.
   If the shape is genuinely unknown, define a type for what you do know.

2. No console.log. Use logger.debug/info/warn/error from src/utils/logger.ts.
   ESLint enforces this with "no-console": "error".

3. Never access import.meta.env.VITE_* directly in components.
   Always use the constants exported from src/utils/constants.ts.

4. Never format numbers inline in components.
   All price, percentage, date, and share formatting goes through src/utils/format.ts.

5. Every data-fetching component must handle all three states: loading, error, success.
   Pattern: if (isLoading) => skeleton | if (isError) => ErrorState | if (empty) => EmptyState | data.
   Never render a blank panel during loading.

6. Every page must be wrapped in PageErrorBoundary.
   Every chart must be wrapped in ChartErrorBoundary.
   A crash in one component must never blank the whole app.

7. M&M.NS must always be URL-encoded when used in URL segments or query strings.
   Call encodeURIComponent(symbol) in every apiClient.get() call and every navigate() call.
   Decode with decodeURIComponent() when reading from useParams().

8. Never call API functions directly from components.
   All API calls go through React Query hooks in src/hooks/. Components use hooks only.

9. Never hardcode strings that the backend also defines.
   Signal types, statuses, directions, strategy names — import from src/types/.

10. Filter state on list pages must be synced to URL query params.
    Filters must survive page refresh and support shareable URLs.
    Use useFilterUrlSync for all filter state management.

11. Text inputs and sliders that trigger API calls must be debounced at 300ms.
    Use useDebounce from src/hooks/useDebounce.ts. Never fire a query on every keystroke.

12. Feature flags control both routing AND UI rendering.
    When FEATURES.shortSignals is false, the Direction column, Direction filter, and
    SHORT-related labels must not appear anywhere in the UI — not disabled, not greyed, absent.

