## 26. AUTHENTICATION AND ONBOARDING FLOW

First visit (no API key in localStorage):
1. App.tsx renders ApiKeySetupScreen — full page, no sidebar/topbar.
2. User enters key => frontend calls GET /api/v1/health to validate.
3. On 200: saves key to identity store, navigates to /.
4. On 401: shows inline error "Invalid key". On network error: shows server URL.

Mid-session 401 (key rotated in backend):
1. Axios response interceptor dispatches tn:auth-failure custom event.
2. AppShell opens ApiKeyModal — full-screen, not dismissible, no backdrop click.
3. User re-enters valid key => modal closes, app continues.

AuthGuard wraps all routes inside AppShell.
If apiKey === '', redirects to /setup.

The user UUID (userId) is auto-generated once on first visit and never shown to the user.
It is sent as X-User-Id with every request.

