## 27. API CLIENT RULES

src/api/client.ts is the single Axios instance. Rules:
- Request interceptor injects X-API-Key and X-User-Id on every request.
- Response interceptor unwraps the { success, data, error } envelope.
  Downstream code receives only data.
- On success: false from backend: rejects with the error message string.
- On HTTP 401: dispatches tn:auth-failure event.
- Never create a second Axios instance. All API calls use this one.
- Timeout: 15 seconds.

API module files wrap one resource each. They return typed promises.
Never call apiClient from components directly — always through a React Query hook.

encodeURIComponent(symbol) must appear in every stocksApi.detail(),
stocksApi.history(), and favoritesApi.remove() call. Never skip it.

