## 28. STATE MANAGEMENT RULES

TanStack Query — all server state. Never store server data in Zustand.
Zustand — all client-only state (apiKey, userId, theme, UI flags). Never fetch data in Zustand.

Cache stale times:
- Active signals: 5min | Signal list: 2min | Stock detail: 5min
- History/candles: 30min | Favorites: 30sec | Paper trading: 5min
- Backtest: 10min | Health check: 60sec (polling)

refetchOnWindowFocus: false on all queries except favorites and health.
Traders switch tabs constantly — surprise re-fetches during the trading day are disruptive.

Mutations must use optimistic updates for favorites add/remove:
1. onMutate: cancel queries, snapshot previous data, apply optimistic change.
2. onError: roll back to snapshot.
3. onSettled: invalidate to sync with server truth.

placeholderData: (prev) => prev on all paginated queries.
Prevents content flash when changing pages.

---

## 29. ROUTING RULES

- /setup — ApiKeySetupScreen. No auth guard. No app shell.
- All other routes — wrapped in AuthGuard inside AppShell.
- Feature-flagged routes redirect to / when flag is off: never render disabled.
- Symbol in StockDetail URL: always URL-encoded in navigate(), always decoded with
  decodeURIComponent(params.symbol) before use.

---

## 30. ERROR BOUNDARY HIERARCHY

Three levels. Must not be collapsed or removed.

RootErrorBoundary       <- full-page fallback, "Reload app" button
  AppShell
    PageErrorBoundary   <- per route, keeps sidebar/topbar alive
      PageComponent
        ChartErrorBoundary  <- chart only, keeps rest of page alive
          CandlestickChart

Every Route element in App.tsx must be wrapped in PageErrorBoundary.
Every chart component must be wrapped in ChartErrorBoundary at its call site.

---

## 31. LOADING STATE STANDARDS

Follow this table without exception:

Scenario                             | Component
First load, no cached data           | LoadingSkeleton — matches layout of expected content
Background refetch, cached data      | Subtle spinner in topbar corner only
Table page change                    | Row skeletons via placeholderData — existing data stays
Chart loading                        | LoadingSkeleton height="300px"
Mutation in progress                 | Button disabled + spinner + text changes ("Adding...")
Empty results (after load complete)  | EmptyState — only when !isLoading && data.length === 0

The universal pattern — use in every data-dependent component:
  if (isLoading) return <LoadingSkeleton variant="table-row" rows={5} />;
  if (isError)   return <ErrorState message={friendlyError(error.message)} onRetry={refetch} />;
  if (!data?.items.length) return <EmptyState message="..." />;
  return <DataComponent data={data.items} />;

---

## 32. FILTER AND PAGINATION RULES

Debounce timing:
- Text inputs, symbol search, confidence slider => 300ms via useDebounce
- Date pickers, multi-select pills, toggles => no debounce

URL sync (all filter state on list pages):
Use useFilterUrlSync hook. Write every filter to URL query params on change.
Delete param when value is default/empty (keep URLs clean).
Always reset page to 1 when any non-page filter changes.

Pagination defaults:
- Default page size: 20 (matches PAGINATION.defaultPageSize in constants)
- Available sizes: 20, 50, 100
- Page size persisted in URL (?limit=50)

---

## 33. FEATURE FLAG RULES

All flag decisions go through src/utils/featureFlags.ts. Never check FEATURES.* directly
in component JSX — always call the named function from featureFlags.

When a flag is off:
- Route: redirect to /, never render disabled/greyed page
- Sidebar item: absent entirely
- Table column: filtered out of the columns array, never rendered as hidden
- Filter option: not in the dropdown/pills list

Correct pattern — filter from array:
  const columns = [
    ...baseColumns,
    featureFlags.showShortDirection() && directionColumn,
  ].filter(Boolean);

Wrong pattern — never do this:
  {FEATURES.shortSignals && <DirectionColumn />}

---

## 34. CHART RULES

CandlestickChart:
- Data limit: cap at 500 candles before passing to chart (via useMemo + slice(-500)).
- Memoize chartData with useMemo([candles]). Re-render only when candles reference changes.
- Destroy chart instance in useEffect cleanup on unmount.
- Chart theme follows app theme (dark/light).
- Wrap in ChartErrorBoundary.

EMA colours (immutable):
- EMA 20: #3B82F6 (blue)
- EMA 50: #F97316 (orange)
- EMA 200: #A855F7 (purple)

EquityCurveChart:
- Only closed paper trades (status === 'CLOSED'). Open trades excluded.
- Sort by exit_date ascending before computing running sum.
- Memoize with useMemo([closedTrades]).

