## 36. FRONTEND LOGGING RULES

src/utils/logger.ts — four methods with environment-aware behaviour:
- logger.debug / logger.info — no-ops in production (unless VITE_DEBUG_MODE=true)
- logger.warn / logger.error — always fire in all environments

The Axios interceptors use logger.debug for every request/response in development.
Never call console.* directly anywhere — ESLint rule "no-console": "error" enforces this.

---

## 37. FRONTEND TESTING RULES

- Unit tests: colocated as *.test.tsx or in __tests__/ subfolders.
- Integration tests: full page renders inside QueryClientProvider + MemoryRouter + RootErrorBoundary.
- ALL API calls mocked with MSW (src/mocks/handlers.ts). Never hit a live backend in tests.
- Chart libraries (lightweight-charts, recharts) are mocked in tests.
  Test the data transformation, not the library rendering.
- localStorage persistence: test the store logic, not the storage mechanism.

Must test:
- format.ts — all functions with edge cases (zero, negative, large INR values)
- useMarketStatus — IST timezone logic, weekend, pipeline run detection
- useFilterUrlSync — URL read/write, page reset on filter change
- featureFlags — all flags off => correct absence in UI
- SignalBadge — all signal_type + direction combinations + flag interaction
- Chart data transforms — 500-candle cap, equity curve running sum
- ApiKeySetupScreen — empty key => stays on screen; 401 => inline error; 200 => enters app
- PageErrorBoundary — component crash shows ErrorState, not blank page

---

## 38. FRONTEND WHAT NOT TO DO

- Do not use any. Use unknown and narrow.
- Do not call console.log — use logger.
- Do not access import.meta.env outside constants.ts.
- Do not format numbers in JSX — use format.ts.
- Do not call API functions from components — use hooks.
- Do not store server state in Zustand — use TanStack Query.
- Do not render feature-flagged content as greyed-out or disabled — remove it entirely.
- Do not skip encodeURIComponent on symbol values in URLs.
- Do not skip error boundaries on pages or charts.
- Do not render EmptyState before loading is complete.
- Do not fire API calls on every keystroke — debounce text inputs and sliders at 300ms.
- Do not add a new npm package without updating the frontend document.
- Do not add a new page without wrapping it in PageErrorBoundary and an AuthGuard route.
- Do not call useIdentityStore to read the API key in components — the Axios interceptor
  handles injection. Components never touch the raw key.

