## 39. DOCUMENT SYNC RULE

Both technical documents are sources of truth. They must stay in sync with the code.

When a change touches the backend, update backend_technical_document.md in the same session.
When a change touches the frontend, update frontend_technical_document.md in the same session.
When a change touches both (new API field shown in UI), update both documents.

Changes that require a backend document update:
- DB schema (table, column, index) + new migration file
- Pipeline step sequence or count
- API endpoint (path, params, response shape)
- Backend environment variable (added, renamed, removed)
- Scoring weights or gate thresholds
- Strategy entry conditions or signal calculation
- Error class hierarchy

Changes that require a frontend document update:
- New component added to the component library
- New page added
- New hook with non-obvious caching behaviour
- New environment variable (VITE_*)
- Feature flag added or removed
- Type changed to match a backend API change
- Formatting rule changed

Do not mark a task complete if the code and any document are out of sync.
